\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.9}{\ignorespaces The pooled MLE fits avalanche area well, suggesting this form of finite size scaling is appropriate. Avalanche size and length appear to have more degraded fits compared with the unpooled fit in Figure \ref {fig:stretched_unpooled_fit}. Select lattice sizes $L = 5, 30, 100$ are displayed - the full data fits are depicted in Appendix Figure \ref {fig:APPENDIX_pooled_stretched_powerlaw_mle_viz}. MLEs are drawn as black points with a connecting line drawn for illustration purposes. The left column shows avalanche size, the centre column shows avalanche area, and the right column shows avalanche $L_1$ length. The dashed vertical lines illustrate the bounding parameter $x_{max}$.}}{22}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
